"""Fixed-arena Vulkan resident-2D vertical slice and device evidence.

Plan step 3 of the GPU scheduler hardening arc. The arena is created once with
a bounded `DrawIrPackedGenerationStoreV3` and is never grown: every frame
reuses the same slots through admit -> write -> seal -> publish -> take ->
complete. Two properties are the point of the slice and are counted, not
asserted in prose:

- `semantic_rebuilds` stays 0 while an exact retained row snapshot is
  unchanged. A bounded rows-only fold is only a fast prefilter; it is never a
  correctness key.
- `readbacks` stays 0: no framebuffer is copied back per frame. The separately
  named proof counter records the single four-byte diagnostic readback.

The retained scene buffer is descriptor-bound to a two-binding SPIR-V checksum
consumer. One explicit proof-buffer readback after fence retirement provides a
collision-limited attestation that at least one accepted shader dispatch read
the packed rows; it does not prove collision-free content identity or that
every accepted dispatch executed. Uploads still use the provider's blocking
staging transfer only when scene bytes change. The current provider also waits
inside every fenced submit; counters expose that unresolved async blocker
instead of labeling the calls nonblocking. Returned fence handles are retained
in bounded batches and released at a batch, mutation, or shutdown boundary.

Non-admission rule: a receipt produced here is routing evidence only. Device
execution still requires the separate evidence qualification bar (including
device timestamps), even when shader consumption is proven by the checksum.
"""

use common.gpu.engine2d.gpu_epoch.{
